llama: keep the backend scheduler on re-reserve (port of upstream #28872)

sched_reserve() recreated ggml_backend_sched whenever sched_need_reserve
was set. With --backend-sampling, llama-server's slot reset detaches the
sampler after each request, so the next request set the flag and freed and
reallocated every compute buffer and the pinned host input buffer.
ggml_backend_sched_reserve() on the existing scheduler re-plans the splits
and only grows buffers; max_nodes depends only on n_ubatch and the model.

diff --git a/src/llama-context.cpp b/src/llama-context.cpp
index 07b4c6148..d36d6146d 100644
--- a/src/llama-context.cpp
+++ b/src/llama-context.cpp
@@ -640,7 +640,12 @@ void llama_context::sched_reserve() {
     gf_res_reserve.reset(new llm_graph_result(max_nodes));
     gf_res_prev_active = nullptr;
 
-    sched.reset(ggml_backend_sched_new(backend_ptrs.data(), backend_buft.data(), backend_ptrs.size(), max_nodes, cparams.pipeline_parallel, cparams.op_offload));
+    // Keep an existing scheduler. llama-server calls llama_set_sampler() for every request, and a new scheduler
+    // frees and reallocates every compute buffer and the pinned host input buffer each time.
+    // ggml_backend_sched_reserve() re-plans the splits and only grows the buffers. Upstream PR #28872.
+    if (!sched) {
+        sched.reset(ggml_backend_sched_new(backend_ptrs.data(), backend_buft.data(), backend_ptrs.size(), max_nodes, cparams.pipeline_parallel, cparams.op_offload));
+    }
 
     llama_memory_context_ptr mctx;
     if (memory) {
